                  <p>
                    <strong>Chapter 2</strong>
                  </p>
                  <h1>Habitat &amp; range</h1>
                  <p>
                    <em>What otters need from a watercourse, and where to expect them on each continent.</em>
                  </p>
                  <ac:adf-extension>
                    <ac:adf-node type="panel">
                      <ac:adf-attribute key="panel-type">note</ac:adf-attribute>
                      <ac:adf-content>
                        <p>
                          <strong>TL;DR</strong>
                        </p>
                        <p>Otters need clean water, abundant prey (fish, crustaceans, molluscs), and dense bankside cover for holts. Pollution and habitat fragmentation are the principal threats.</p>
                      </ac:adf-content>
                    </ac:adf-node>
                  </ac:adf-extension>
                  <h2>Freshwater requirements</h2>
                  <p>Most species are tightly tied to clean rivers, lakes, and wetlands. Indicator-species status: an otter population implies a functioning aquatic ecosystem.</p>
                  <ac:task-list>
                    <ac:task>
                      <ac:task-status>incomplete</ac:task-status>
                      <ac:task-body>
                        <span>Clean water with low heavy-metal load</span>
                      </ac:task-body>
                    </ac:task>
                    <ac:task>
                      <ac:task-status>incomplete</ac:task-status>
                      <ac:task-body>
                        <span>Dense bankside vegetation for holts</span>
                      </ac:task-body>
                    </ac:task>
                    <ac:task>
                      <ac:task-status>incomplete</ac:task-status>
                      <ac:task-body>
                        <span>Year-round fish biomass</span>
                      </ac:task-body>
                    </ac:task>
                    <ac:task>
                      <ac:task-status>incomplete</ac:task-status>
                      <ac:task-body>
                        <span>Connectivity between waterbodies</span>
                      </ac:task-body>
                    </ac:task>
                  </ac:task-list>
                  <h2>Marine habitat</h2>
                  <p>Sea otters favour kelp-forest coastlines with shallow rocky reefs and urchin populations. They rarely come ashore.</p>
                  <h2>Continental ranges</h2>
                  <p>Otters occupy every continent except Australia and Antarctica. Densest populations remain in the Amazon, Congo basin, and Pacific Northwest.</p>
                </ac:layout-cell>
