    'bodies': list([
      dict({
        'body_preview': '''
          <ac:layout>
              <ac:layout-section ac:type="fixed-width">
                <ac:layout-cell>
                  <p>
                    <strong>Component showcase</strong>
                  </p>
                  <h1>An editorial frame for AI-authored documents.</h1>
                  <p>
                    <em>Every tag, every variant, in one document — the way a real richdoc should be read top-to-bottom.</em>
                  </p>
                  <p>
                    <em>v0.4 · Updated this build · Platform team</em>
                  </p>
                  <table data-layout="default">
                    <colgroup>
                      <col style="width: 200.0px;"/>
                      <col style="width: 760.0px;"/>
                    </colgroup>
                    <tbody>
                      <tr>
                        <th>
                          <p>
                            <strong>Audience</strong>
                          </p>
                        </th>
                        <td>
                          <p>Agents writing for humans</p>
                        </td>
                      </tr>
                      <tr>
                        <th>
                          <p>
                            <strong>Vocabulary</strong>
                          </p>
                        </th>
                        <td>
                          <p>~70 tags · 40+ components</p>
                        </td>
                      </tr>
                      <tr>
                        <th>
                          <p>
                            <strong>Status</strong>
                          </p>
                        </th>
                        <td>
                          <p>
                            <ac:structured-macro ac:name="status" ac:schema-version="1">
                              <ac:parameter ac:name="title">stable</ac:parameter>
                              <ac:parameter ac:name="colour">Green</ac:parameter>
                            </ac:structured-macro>
                            <ac:structured-macro ac:name="status" ac:schema-version="1">
                              <ac:parameter ac:name="title">expanded vocabulary</ac:parameter>
                              <ac:parameter ac:name="colour">Blue</ac:parameter>
                            </ac:structured-macro>
                          </p>
                        </td>
                      </tr>
                    </tbody>
                  </table>
                  <ac:adf-extension>
                    <ac:adf-node type="panel">
                      <ac:adf-attribute key="panel-type">note</ac:adf-attribute>
                      <ac:adf-content>
                        <p>
                          <strong>TL;DR</strong>
                        </p>
                        <p><em>Richdoc</em> is a small framework for documents written by an agent and read by a person in a browser. This page exercises every tag in the vocabulary the way a real document should — read top-to-bottom, with occasional asides dropping down to a Notes section at the foot of the page.</p>
                      </ac:adf-content>
                    </ac:adf-node>
                  </ac:adf-extension>
                  <ac:adf-extension>
                    <ac:adf-node type="panel">
                      <ac:adf-attribute key="panel-type">info</ac:adf-attribute>
                      <ac:adf-content>
                        <p>
                          <strong>Reader controls (bottom-right cog)</strong>
                        </p>
                        <p>Every richdoc ships with a floating <strong>preview picker</strong> in the bottom-right corner. Open it to switch between the two themes (<em>Editorial</em> / <em>Graphite</em>), three modes (<em>Light</em> / <em>Dark</em> / <em>Auto</em>), and four page widths (<em>Narrow</em> / <em>Standard</em> / <em>Wide</em> / <em>Full</em>). Your choices persist per file. Suppress the picker with <code>&lt;rd-page prefs="off"&gt;</code>.</p>
                        <p>Squeeze the page to <strong>Narrow</strong> in a wide browser to see the multi-column layouts, stat tiles, and TOC adapt to the chosen content width — responsiveness is driven by container queries on <code>rd-page</code>, not the viewport.</p>
                      </ac:adf-content>
                    </ac:adf-node>
                  </ac:adf-extension>
                  <p>The look is intentionally editorial: warm paper, Fraunces display, Geist body, hairlines instead of cards, oldstyle figures, and the occasional pull-quote.</p>
                  <h2>Callouts</h2>
                  <p>Five callout types, each with a Lucide icon and tracked small-caps title. They are quieter than the old filled blocks — a tinted background and a 2 px left rule do the work.</p>
                  <ac:adf-extension>
                    <ac:adf-node type="panel">
                      <ac:adf-attribute key="panel-type">info</ac:adf-attribute>
                      <ac:adf-content>
                        <p>
                          <strong>What this is</strong>
                        </p>
                        <p>Callouts break out short asides — context, caveats, or pointers — that you do not want buried in a paragraph.</p>
                      </ac:adf-content>
                    </ac:adf-node>
                  </ac:adf-extension>
                  <ac:adf-extension>
                    <ac:adf-node type="panel">
                      <ac:adf-attribute key="panel-type">success</ac:adf-attribute>
                      <ac:adf-content>
                        <p>
                          <strong>Recommended</strong>
                        </p>
                        <p>Prefer callouts over bold-italic emphasis for anything more than a sentence.</p>
                      </ac:adf-content>
                    </ac:adf-node>
                  </ac:adf-extension>
                  <ac:adf-extension>
                    <ac:adf-node type="panel">
                      <ac:adf-attribute key="panel-type">warning</ac:adf-attribute>
                      <ac:adf-content>
                        <p>
                          <strong>Heads up</strong>
                        </p>
                        <p><code>rd-cols</code> collapses to a single column under ~720 px. Do not put more than four columns or content becomes unreadable on tablets.</p>
                      </ac:adf-content>
                    </ac:adf-node>
                  </ac:adf-extension>
                  <ac:adf-extension>
                    <ac:adf-node type="panel">
                      <ac:adf-attribute key="panel-type">error</ac:adf-attribute>
                      <ac:adf-content>
                        <p>
                          <strong>Don't</strong>
                        </p>
                        <p>Never invent new <code>rd-*</code> tags. The linter fails and the rendered doc shows empty boxes.</p>
                      </ac:adf-content>
                    </ac:adf-node>
                  </ac:adf-extension>
                  <ac:adf-extension>
                    <ac:adf-node type="panel">
                      <ac:adf-attribute key="panel-type">note</ac:adf-attribute>
                      <ac:adf-content>
                        <p>Title is optional. Without one, the callout uses the type name as a fallback heading.</p>
                      </ac:adf-content>
                    </ac:adf-node>
                  </ac:adf-extension>
                  <h2>Cards in columns</h2>
                  <p>Use <code>rd-cols</code> for genuinely parallel content. Cards are the natural child. Each accent value lights up a top rule and a coloured kicker label so the card reads typographically, not as a tinted block.</p>
                  <h3>Three cards, no accents</h3>
                </ac:layout-cell>
              </ac:layout-section>
              <ac:layout-section ac:type="three_equal" ac:breakout-mode="default">
                <ac:layout-cell>
                  <ac:adf-extension>
                    <ac:adf-node type="panel">
                      <ac:adf-attribute key="panel-type">note</ac:adf-attribute>
                      <ac:adf-content>
                        <p>
                          <strong>Discovery</strong>
                        </p>
                        <p>Find out what exists. Read the code, run small probes, talk to whoever knows the system best.</p>
                      </ac:adf-content>
                    </ac:adf-node>
                  </ac:adf-extension>
                </ac:layout-cell>
                <ac:layout-cell>
                  <ac:adf-extension>
                    <ac:adf-node type="panel">
                      <ac:adf-attribute key="panel-type">note</ac:adf-attribute>
                      <ac:adf-content>
                        <p>
                          <strong>Design</strong>
                        </p>
                        <p>Decide what to change. Resolve the trade-offs explicitly. Write them down before touching anything.</p>
                      </ac:adf-content>
                    </ac:adf-node>
                  </ac:adf-extension>
                </ac:layout-cell>
                <ac:layout-cell>
                  <ac:adf-extension>
                    <ac:adf-node type="panel">
                      <ac:adf-attribute key="panel-type">note</ac:adf-attribute>
                      <ac:adf-content>
                        <p>
                          <strong>Delivery</strong>
                        </p>
                        <p>Execute the plan in reviewable units. Keep changes small and traceable. Ship boring code.</p>
                      </ac:adf-content>
                    </ac:adf-node>
                  </ac:adf-extension>
                </ac:layout-cell>
              </ac:layout-section>
              <ac:layout-section ac:type="fixed-width">
                <ac:layout-cell>
                  <h3>Four cards with accent colours</h3>
                </ac:layout-cell>
              </ac:layout-section>
              <ac:layout-section ac:type="two_equal" ac:breakout-mode="default">
                <ac:layout-cell>
                  <ac:adf-extension>
                    <ac:adf-node type="panel">
                      <ac:adf-attribute key="panel-type">info</ac:adf-attribute>
                      <ac:adf-content>
                        <p>
                          <strong>Info</strong>
                        </p>
