                        <span>Add p99 latency dashboard <em>(@kim, due 2026-05-12)</em></span>
                      </ac:task-body>
                    </ac:task>
                  </ac:task-list>
                  <h2>In progress</h2>
                  <ac:task-list>
                    <ac:task>
                      <ac:task-status>incomplete</ac:task-status>
                      <ac:task-body>
                        <span>Refresh-failure spike investigation (see callout below) <em>(@dana, due 2026-05-15)</em></span>
                      </ac:task-body>
                    </ac:task>
                    <ac:task>
                      <ac:task-status>incomplete</ac:task-status>
                      <ac:task-body>
                        <span>Webauthn support behind a feature flag <em>(@kim, due 2026-05-17)</em></span>
                      </ac:task-body>
                    </ac:task>
                    <ac:task>
                      <ac:task-status>incomplete</ac:task-status>
                      <ac:task-body>
                        <span>Migrate session store to Postgres 16 <em>(@dana, due 2026-05-20)</em></span>
                      </ac:task-body>
                    </ac:task>
                  </ac:task-list>
                  <ac:adf-extension>
                    <ac:adf-node type="panel">
                      <ac:adf-attribute key="panel-type">warning</ac:adf-attribute>
                      <ac:adf-content>
                        <p>
                          <strong>Refresh-failure spike</strong>
                        </p>
                        <p>Refresh failures climbed from ~320/day to 412/day this week (+27%). Early signal: about 60% of failures share a small set of UA strings consistent with one mobile build that's caching tokens past expiry.</p>
                        <p><strong>Plan:</strong> reach out to the mobile lead, gather build numbers, and decide whether to ship a server-side mitigation or wait for the next mobile release.</p>
                      </ac:adf-content>
                    </ac:adf-node>
                  </ac:adf-extension>
                  <h2>Risks</h2>
                </ac:layout-cell>
              </ac:layout-section>
              <ac:layout-section ac:type="two_equal" ac:breakout-mode="default">
                <ac:layout-cell>
                  <ac:adf-extension>
                    <ac:adf-node type="panel">
                      <ac:adf-attribute key="panel-type">warning</ac:adf-attribute>
                      <ac:adf-content>
                        <p>
                          <strong>Key-rotation downtime window</strong>
                        </p>
                        <p>Production rotation is scheduled for 2026-05-21 03:00 UTC. JWKS cache TTL is 5 min; we expect a ≤5min window where some clients still trust the old key. Mitigation: pre-warm the new key at JWKS for 24h ahead.</p>
                      </ac:adf-content>
                    </ac:adf-node>
                  </ac:adf-extension>
                </ac:layout-cell>
                <ac:layout-cell>
                  <ac:adf-extension>
                    <ac:adf-node type="panel">
                      <ac:adf-attribute key="panel-type">info</ac:adf-attribute>
                      <ac:adf-content>
                        <p>
                          <strong>Postgres 16 migration</strong>
                        </p>
                        <p>Cutover is dual-write for 48h then primary switch. Rollback path: flip a single DSN and replay the WAL.</p>
                      </ac:adf-content>
                    </ac:adf-node>
                  </ac:adf-extension>
                </ac:layout-cell>
              </ac:layout-section>
              <ac:layout-section ac:type="fixed-width">
                <ac:layout-cell>
                  <h2>Decisions logged</h2>
                  <ac:structured-macro ac:name="expand">
                    <ac:parameter ac:name="title">Refresh-token rotation: opaque vs JWT</ac:parameter>
                    <ac:rich-text-body>
                      <p>We picked <strong>opaque</strong> refresh tokens stored server-side. Reasoning: refresh tokens get reused, replayed, and revoked far more than access tokens; the size and signature cost of JWT buys us nothing for that role.</p>
                      <p>Access tokens remain JWT (EdDSA) so service-to-service paths stay stateless.</p>
                    </ac:rich-text-body>
                  </ac:structured-macro>
                  <ac:structured-macro ac:name="expand">
                    <ac:parameter ac:name="title">Why we deferred OAuth device flow</ac:parameter>
                    <ac:rich-text-body>
                      <p>One first-party client requested device flow for a CLI tool. We deferred — the use case is satisfied by a long-lived API token with scope restrictions, which is simpler and already supported. Revisit in Q3 if a second client asks.</p>
                    </ac:rich-text-body>
                  </ac:structured-macro>
                  <h2>Next two weeks</h2>
                  <ul>
                    <li><strong>2026-05-15</strong> — Refresh-failure mitigation decided — Either ship server-side fix or commit to mobile-only fix and accept the spike.</li>
                    <li><strong>2026-05-17</strong> — Webauthn behind flag — Internal users only. Public flip targeted for the following sprint.</li>
                    <li><strong>2026-05-20</strong> — Postgres 16 dual-write begins — 48h soak. Cutover the morning of 2026-05-22.</li>
                    <li><strong>2026-05-21 03:00 UTC</strong> — Key rotation in production — JWKS pre-warmed since 2026-05-20.</li>
                  </ul>
                </ac:layout-cell>
              </ac:layout-section>
            </ac:layout>
